  message: "Fixed in PR #2347 (60d178eaf 'napi keeps every function a JS name is registered to'). Root cause: the C/C++ files were iterated as a set and the export map was keyed by JS name, last writer wins. Fix: every registration of a name keeps its own edge, to the function in its own file. Re-ran the filed repro on dev 49bc5c6e4: five .c files registering 'hello', PYTHONHASHSEED 1 to 6: each seed gives the same 5 edges, one to each of impl_a..impl_e (filed: one edge, to impl_e, impl_b, impl_b, impl_a, impl_c, impl_a). Production-path test: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_linker_hash_seed_order.py (four processes under distinct seeds). Corpus impact was not measured when filed and is not measured now. Outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/closure/ (fixtures*.txt, trees_summary.txt, pair_check_dev.txt)."  # 74eb
